# Backend Rules


## Stack


Use:

- Ruby on Rails API only
- PostgreSQL
- Redis
- Sidekiq
- Devise
- Devise JWT
- JWT
- Pundit
- Versionist
- Interactor
- Jbuilder
- Active Storage
- Resend


## Rails Principles


Follow Rails conventions.


Controllers must remain thin.


Controllers handle:

- authentication
- authorization
- params
- rendering


Controllers must NOT contain:

- business logic
- complex queries
- workflows


## Business Logic


Use Interactors.


Examples:


CreateStudent

UpdateGrade

RecordAttendance

GenerateReport


Interactors handle:

- workflows
- transactions
- business operations


## Models


Active Record models handle:

- associations
- validations
- scopes


Use Rails validations.


Never create separate validator classes.


Example:


validates :email, presence: true


## Authorization


Use:

Pundit


Every protected action requires authorization.


Example:


authorize @student


## API


All APIs must be versioned.


Format:


/api/v1


Use:

Jbuilder


Return consistent JSON.


## Background Jobs


Use:

Sidekiq


Jobs:

- emails
- reports
- notifications
- exports


## Email


Use:

Resend


Templates required for:

- welcome
- password reset
- attendance
- grades
- announcements